refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.returnvalues;
Returns the value of the requested attribute, or &false; on failure.
The value of some attributes, such as PDO::ATTR_PERSISTENT, can itself be &false;, so a &false; return value does not always indicate a failure.

&reftitle.errors;

 PDO::getAttribute may throw a PDOException
 when the underlying driver does not support the requested attribute.

&reftitle.changelog;
&Version; &Description;
8.4.0
It is now possible to fetch the value of the PDO::ATTR_STRINGIFY_FETCHES attribute.
8.4.0
The value of PDO::ATTR_AUTOCOMMIT is now returned as bool by the MySQL and Firebird drivers, and the value of PDO::ATTR_EMULATE_PREPARES and PDO::MYSQL_ATTR_DIRECT_QUERY is now returned as bool by the MySQL driver; previously, they were returned as int.

  &reftitle.examples;



    Retrieving database connection attributes


<?php
$pdo = new PDO('sqlite::memory:');

$attributes = [
    'DRIVER_NAME', 'ERRMODE', 'CASE', 'ORACLE_NULLS', 'PERSISTENT',
    'CLIENT_VERSION', 'SERVER_VERSION', 'AUTOCOMMIT', 'TIMEOUT',
];

foreach ($attributes as $name) {
    try {
        $value = $pdo->getAttribute(constant("PDO::ATTR_$name"));
        echo "PDO::ATTR_$name: ", var_export($value, true), "\n";
    } catch (PDOException $e) {
        echo "PDO::ATTR_$name: ", $e->getMessage(), "\n";
    }
}
?>


